      "webpage": {
        "text": "Quick hits\n\n'Pirates of the Caribbean: Dead Man's Chest'\n\nRELEASED: July 7\n\nMPAA RATING: PG-13\n\nMY THOUGHTS: In this film starring Johnny Depp, Orlando Bloom and Keira Knightley, action and suspense hold the story together and keep the viewer entranced, while comedic performances provide ample entertainment.\n\nThe plot takes several twists that leave viewers confused, so it would be a good idea to see it twice before trying to make sense of it. Otherwise, it is amusing. The third installment will be released next year.\n\nGRADE: B\n\n- Justin Conklin\n\n'Tomb Raider: Legend'\n\nRELEASED: April 11\n\nPLATFORMS: PlayStation2, PSP, Xbox and Xbox 360\n\nESRB RATING: Teen\n\nMY THOUGHTS: Lara Croft goes around the globe from Bolivia to Kazakhstan on her never-ending search for treasures in this installment of the Tomb Raider series. Thanks to new game developers (Crystal Dynamics), the graphics look more realistic and characters maneuver more smoothly without being bound by those awful pixels.\n\nThough game play generally is less frustrating, an experienced tomb raider will find the game disappointingly short. Though full of the obligatory cool new items, puzzles and moves, Legend is pretty much the same game that it was 10 years ago. That's good news for fans who just want more Tomb Raider: more ancient ruins, hidden keys and impossible jumps.\n\nGRADE: A-\n\n- Katharine Diehl",
        "metadata": {
          "title": "Quick hits"
        },
        "credits": 2
      },
